<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Wave C ~ the hearth-stone carries the name

Wave C builds `K15` step 6, the fence, under one identity model the operator approved on 2026-10-20: //sync carries; verification decides// (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> #/rulings; the research at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/research/identity-invariants-2026">>). Beneath it stands the moʻolelo's first line: the truth rests in the minds of the operators, and the CRDTs carry it to the synced stores. Wave C launches once Wave B lands on a green span; `W26`'s slices 3, 4 and 6 run beside it on the floor's own ground; its slice 5 follows, since the accepted floor rests as a face's D row.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-stories>>

!! The stories

''Kalani's laptop forgets nothing it swore to.'' Someone with write access to Kalani's synced docs rewrites the daemon doc to name another face's group and KEL prefix, with a perfectly valid edge from that other face. Kalani's laptop boots, reads its own sealed anchor, sees a bundle it never swore to, and refuses by name. The crier shouted a lie; the stone kept the name.

''The Council's lease never runs backward.'' A stale replica of the Council's daemon doc arrives missing the newest lease slot. Before Wave C, an old device edge reads current against it. After it, each device keeps a sealed frontier that never falls, and the stale replica moves nothing.

''A tab knows its face before it speaks.'' Kalani opens a tab; it reads the face's pins from its custody anchor at unlock, never from a document, then proves itself to the holder. The tab's own Repo retires; each face's house Repo serves its documents.

''Two faces, two shelves of books.'' Kalani's browser wears their own face and the Council's, each with its own social planes keyed by its PersonaGroup, as the node already holds them.

''The myth.'' The village crier runs fast and everywhere, and wrong whenever the last shout lied. A family's true name stays carved in its own hearth-stone, where only founding, admission or recovery may carve. The crier repeats the stone; no shout changes it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-reds>>

!! The reds ~ grounds before wins, each written as the specification, all proven at the wave's end

# ''The sealed anchor.'' Each face holds, on each device, a D row: its PersonaGroup, persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Founding, admission and the recovery rites write it; sync never does. Red: a forged selector row in the daemon doc, then a coherent valid foreign bundle, switch no pinned face; a missing anchor refuses face boot by name.
# ''The signed `@persona` log.'' Founding and admission acts, device edges and lease advances travel as signed entries in the face's `@persona` plane, verified against the anchor and the KEL; the reader folds them as the KEL board does. Red: two signed acts at one sequence surface as a fork, never a CRDT winner.
# ''The monotone frontier.'' Lease advances carry signatures in the per-writer shape; the sealed local frontier never falls. Red: a deleted, replayed or unsigned high slot lowers nothing and raises nothing. An act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) refuses a target naming a newer bound than the frontier holds, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under.
# ''Verified projections.'' The face planes and the daemon doc's identity tiddlers read as projections of verified records, disposable and rebuilt. Red: a plane URL with no signed founding or admission act behind it never registers.
# ''The FCK fence.'' Each face's D rows (atom, archive, anchor, custody root, proof keys) seal under that face's own random FCK and key by its PersonaGroup on both hosts; the vessel key opens none of them. Red: K15's isolation red at the key-class level, where Wave B's `test.fails` rows turn green: unlock A alone, and every key A holds, the vessel key included, opens no B row.
# ''The daemon's last unions'' (Wave B's census, node items 4 to 6): one keyhive, face ledger, content-key seat and seat-roll set per face, never one per daemon; face-join and seat duties reseal the asking face's bags alone; CLI selectors name their face and never default to `h0`; `fleet-join-pending` keys by face; a joined face's hearth dial pin stands per face.
# ''One SharedWorker per house.'' A tab knows its face from its custody anchor before it connects, then opens the SharedWorker whose `name` digests that house's (PersonaGroup, persona root); the house's island runs in that worker's own thread and realm, with no nested Worker (Chromium exposes none inside a SharedWorker), so each face keeps its own realm, one island per house, and a house outlives any one of its tabs. Red, in a real browser on every engine: two faces' tabs reach two worker instances, a second tab of one face reaches the same one, and the last tab's close ends the house.
# ''The house holder answers, never stalls'' (Wave B's seventh fresh read, carried). A floor or house worker that never announces `ready` refuses its held asks by name and is never left waiting; a replay posts its replacement manifest before it retires the crossing it replaces; a missing seat-roll ledger keeps one pending find per document, never one per gate read; the C4 boot trace's manifest marker fires on the real source, proven by a control that runs `instrumentBootSource` over the daemon and counts one `host:manifest-post`; the pre-clear `doc:rested` carries a storage proof from the house's own rest shore. Red: each of these, every one through an event or causal read, never a timer that decides.
# ''The tab reads its pins from custody'' and the tab's own Repo retires; ''each face holds its own social planes in the browser'', keyed by PersonaGroup.
# ''The place card.'' Every node joinee holds a place card from its own place founding; a joinee path that reaches a place-arm presentation without one reds, cured at the place founding.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/beside-it>>

!! Beside it ~ the edge frontier

Row `K17`, the signed edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier), shares Wave C's signed-log pattern and builds beside it: the frontier certificate, the genesis frontier at every founding, raise registration, the widening reader, and the admit bundle carrying the frontier. Wave C's anchor and `K17`'s frontier read one verifier style on node and browser.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-crew>>

!! The crew ~ very large work chunks under the mixed-model-swarm protocols

One joint lane (`feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--k15-wave-c`), one pull request, landed whole and merged by train. A Sonnet Episkopos leads; the Codex Sol (`gpt-6-sol`, walled) builds; the Copilot seat (`gpt-5.3-codex`) reads, scouts and sweeps (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm">>). The battery rides CI's shards: locally the wave runs its build and each red's proof against the base tree, pushes once, and reads lane CI, held-out and the shards. A fresh Sol reader, from a lineage that built none of it, reads the whole diff before the train. The scout census opens the lane: every place an identity pin reads from a mutable doc without verification, by file and line, sorted by what inherits shape from what.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

!! Edges ~ held outside Wave C

* ''Transparency and witnesses'' for equivocation across devices: their own row, later.
* ''The far agent's relay seat'': its research after `I1`.
* ''The signer frames each floor duty's domain'': `X0`.
* ''Unsigned `requestedBy` on synced summonses'': `I1` moves summonses onto `@intents`, where each entry carries its own signature.

<<~/ahu>>

